// Unified effect catalog. Four sections, three of them descriptor tables keyed
// by DISTINCT id namespaces that overlap numerically but mean different things
// (86 is the WZ_WATERBALL *skill* and the EFST_EXPLOSIONSPIRITS *status*; 89 is
// the WZ_STORMGUST *skill* and the EF_STORMGUST *special effect*) -- a flat
// merged map would silently collide.
//
//   `efsts`    -- keyed by EFST id. Persistent status auras attached/detached
//                 by `StatusEffectChanged` (`domain/effects/status_visuals.rs`),
//                 and the recipe table `Efst(id)` composition splices from.
//                 `placement`/`ground_anchor` are ignored here.
//   `skills`   -- keyed by rAthena skill id; drives the skill-effect runtime
//                 (`domain/effects/triggers.rs`).
//   `special`  -- the rAthena `e_special_effects` (EF_*) namespace, serving BOTH
//                 the RSW `EFFECT` object's `effect_type` (`spawn_map_effects`,
//                 persistent position-anchored) and aesir's `SpecialEffect`
//                 packets (`on_special_effect`, fire-and-forget at the source
//                 unit); see aesir `Aesir.ZoneServer.Mmo.EffectId`. `placement`
//                 is ignored -- these always anchor at their own position.
//   `shader_fx`-- name-keyed procedural burst table the `Shader(key)` layers
//                 resolve against.
//
// Every descriptor carries an ordered `visuals: [...]` list; the rest of its
// fields (`sound`, `placement`, `color`, `repeating`, `ground_anchor`) apply to
// the entry as a whole. The layer vocabulary:
//
//   Str("x.str" | "x.strfx.ron")  native GRF STR or authored strfx asset.
//   Sprite("이팩트/firewall")       looping SPR/ACT stem under `data/sprite/`.
//   Shader("fire_bolt")           key into `shader_fx` below; validated at load.
//   Bespoke("ice_wall")           key dispatched to code (ice_wall/smoke/
//                                 emitter); never looked up in `shader_fx`.
//   Efst(31)                      splice EFST 31's recipe layers in here.
//
// `Efst(id)` is COMPOSITION, not triggering: it copies the referenced `efsts`
// entry's visual layers into this entry at catalog build time and nothing else
// -- all other fields stay local (this entry's `placement`, `repeating`,
// `color`, `sound` win). It never makes the server apply a status; status
// visuals are driven independently by `StatusEffectChanged` keyed on the EFST
// id. One level deep only: an `efsts` recipe may not itself contain `Efst`
// layers. The catalog build rejects, loudly, a dangling `Efst` ref, a nested
// one, an unknown `Shader` key, and more than one layer of the same kind in a
// resolved descriptor.
//
// Caveats (`special` section):
//   - Only effects backed by an STR asset (or a `Bespoke`/`Shader` layer) can
//     play here. Many classic ambient effects (firefly=45, sandwind=46,
//     torch=47, ...) are hardcoded particle systems in the original client with
//     no STR -- leave them unmapped; they need bespoke emitters, not this path.
//   - Unmapped `effect_type`s are logged by `spawn_map_effects`; use those
//     logs to discover which ids real maps actually reference, then add them
//     here.
(
    efsts: {
        // 19 EFST_KYRIE (aesir Efst.id(:kyrie)) -- Kyrie Eleison's persistent
        // barrier shimmer, driven by StatusEffectChanged(on=true/false). Uses
        // the leaner "_min" GRF variant, not the full one-shot cast STR (id 73
        // in `skills:` below already plays the cast sound, so no sound here).
        19: (
            visuals: [Str("kyrie_min.str")],
            sound: None,
            placement: Caster,
            color: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0),
            repeating: false,
        ),
        // 22 EFST_LEX_AETERNA (aesir Efst.id(:lexaeterna)) -- Lex Aeterna's
        // persistent danger mark hovering above the marked unit (player or
        // mob), driven by StatusEffectChanged rather than the one-shot cast
        // flash in `skills:` below (id 78, `lexaeterna.str`).
        22: (
            visuals: [Str("lex_mark.strfx.ron")],
            sound: None,
            placement: Target,
            color: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0),
            repeating: true,
        ),
        // 31 EFST_ENERGYCOAT (aesir Efst.id(:energycoat)) -- Energy Coat's
        // persistent aura, driven by StatusEffectChanged(on=true/false) rather
        // than the one-shot cast flash in `skills:` below.
        31: (
            visuals: [Str("energycoat.str")],
            sound: None,
            placement: Caster,
            color: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0),
            repeating: false,
        ),
        // 86 EFST_EXPLOSIONSPIRITS (Fury) -- the classic thundershock: brief
        // red lightning arcs (native elec_y_03.bmp) crackling around the
        // sprite for the buff duration, looped, on top of the opt3 red tint.
        // The cast burst is the one-shot explosion_spirits.strfx.ron in
        // `skills:` (id 270). Steel Body (87) and Blade Stop (85) render as
        // opt3 sprite tints only, so they are intentionally absent here.
        86: (
            visuals: [Str("fury_sparks.strfx.ron")],
            sound: None,
            placement: Caster,
            color: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0),
            repeating: true,
        ),
        // --- Crusader auras --------------------------------------------------
        // Shared aura families (shield for 58/59/62, holy for 60/61) plus
        // dedicated Spear Quicken (68) and Shrink (197) loops, each kept
        // distinct through its restrained descriptor tint (architecture:
        // alpha/intensity below one-shot values, finalized in the visual
        // pass). The cast bursts live in `skills:` below.
        58: ( // EFST_AUTOGUARD -- cool blue shield loop.
            visuals: [Str("crusader_shield_aura.strfx.ron")],
            sound: None,
            placement: Caster,
            color: (0.55, 0.75, 1.0, 0.55),
